vaṉ"}]},{"text":"தாய்க்கே","tr":"tāykkē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தாய்க்","tr":"tāyk"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கே","tr":"kē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"கழனி","parts":[{"text":"கழனி","lemma":"கழனி","gloss":"paddy field"}],"gloss":"paddy field"},{"surface":"மாஅத்து","parts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"மா","gloss":"mango tree"},{"text":"அத்து","lemma":"அத்து","gloss":"inflectional suffix"}],"gloss":"of the mango tree"},{"surface":"விளைந்து","parts":[{"text":"விளைந்து","lemma":"விளை","gloss":"having ripened"}],"gloss":"having ripened"},{"surface":"உகு","parts":[{"text":"உகு","lemma":"உகு","gloss":"falling"}],"gloss":"falling"},{"surface":"தீம்பழம்","parts":[{"text":"தீம்","lemma":"தீமை","gloss":"sweet"},{"text":"பழம்","lemma":"பழம்","gloss":"fruit"}],"gloss":"sweet fruit"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பழன","parts":[{"text":"பழன","lemma":"பழன","gloss":"of the pond"}],"gloss":"of the pond","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வாளை","parts":[{"text":"வாளை","lemma":"வாளை","gloss":"scabbard fish"}],"gloss":"scabbard fish"},{"surface":"கதூஉம்","parts":[{"text":"கதூஉம்","lemma":"கதூஉம்","gloss":"which seizes"}],"gloss":"which seizes","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஊரன்","parts":[{"text":"ஊரன்","lemma":"ஊரன்","gloss":"chief of the town"}],"gloss":"chief of the town"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எம்மில்","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"our"},{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"house"}],"gloss":"in our house"},{"surface":"பெருமொழி","parts":[{"text":"பெரு","lemma":"பெரு","gloss":"big"},{"text":"மொழி","lemma":"மொழி","gloss":"words"}],"gloss":"boastful words"},{"surface":"கூறி","parts":[{"text":"கூறி","lemma":"கூறு","gloss":"having spoken"}],"gloss":"having spoken"},{"surface":"தம்மில்","parts":[{"text":"தம்","lemma":"தான்","gloss":"their"},{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"house"}],"gloss":"in their house"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கையும்","parts":[{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"hand"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"hand and"},{"surface":"காலும்","parts":[{"text":"கால்","lemma":"கால்","gloss":"leg"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"leg and"},{"surface":"தூக்க","parts":[{"text":"தூக்க","lemma":"தூக்கு","gloss":"when raised"}],"gloss":"when raised"},{"surface":"தூக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"தூக்கும்","lemma":"தூக்கு","gloss":"raises"}],"gloss":"which raises"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடி","parts":[{"text":"ஆடி","lemma":"ஆடி","gloss":"mirror"}],"gloss":"mirror"},{"surface":"பாவை","parts":[{"text":"பாவை","lemma":"பாவை","gloss":"image"}],"gloss":"image"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல","lemma":"போல்","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மேவன","parts":[{"text":"மேவன","lemma":"மேவு","gloss":"pleasing things"}],"gloss":"pleasing things"},{"surface":"செய்யும்","parts":[{"text":"செய்யும்","lemma":"செய்","gloss":"does"}],"gloss":"who does"},{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"தான்","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"புதல்வன்","parts":[{"text":"புதல்வன்","lemma":"புதல்வன்","gloss":"son"}],"gloss":"son"},{"surface":"தாய்க்கே","parts":[{"text":"தாய்","lemma":"தாய்","gloss":"mother"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"கு","gloss":"to"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"to the mother indeed"}]}],"literal":"Sweet fruit that ripens and falls from the mango tree of the paddy field / the vāḷai fish of the pond seizes, the chief of such a town / in our house, speaking boastful words, but in his own house / when hand and leg are raised, raising them / like a mirror image / does whatever is pleasing to the mother of his son.","translation":"The chief of the town where the vāḷai fish in the pond snaps up the sweet mangoes that ripen and fall from the field's mango tree, speaks boastful words in our house. But in his own house, like a reflection in a mirror that raises its hands and legs whenever they are raised, he does only what is pleasing to the mother of his son.","modern":"வயல்வெளியில் உள்ள மாமரத்திலிருந்து பழுத்து விழும் இனிய பழத்தை குளத்து வாளை மீன் கவ்விக்கொள்ளும் ஊரைச் சேர்ந்த தலைவன், எமது வீட்டில் பெரிய வார்த்தைகளைப் பேசுவான். ஆனால், தன் வீட்டில், கையும் காலும் தூக்கினால் தானும் தூக்கும் கண்ணாடிப் பிம்பத்தைப் போல, தன் மகனின் தாய்க்குப் பிடித்தமானவற்றையே செய்வான்.","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the courtesan (parattai) to her friends, mocking the hero (the chief of the agricultural Marutam region). She points out his hypocrisy: while he boasts of his independence and power when visiting her house, he becomes completely submissive at his own home. She compares him to a mirror image (āṭip pāvai) that mindlessly mimics every movement of the person standing before it, showing how he obeys his wife's every command. The natural description of the vāḷai fish easily catching the sweet mango that falls from the tree serves as an implied metaphor (uḷḷuṟai). It suggests that just as the fish effortlessly enjoys the sweet fruit, the wife easily controls the hero. The key words are 'āṭip pāvai' (mirror image) and 'putalvaṉ tāy' (mother of his son), which emphasize his domestic subservience.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}